          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-21107 build: remove kernel objects in make clean",
        "message": "LU-21107 build: remove kernel objects in make clean\n\nmake clean should remove kernel object files. Previously, it did via\nthe MOSTLYCLEANFILES variable. However, when that variable was\nremoved, nothing was left that cleaned up the kernel modules. This\ncleans them up by delegating to the Kbuild clean target.\n\nThe new target runs for make clean, distclean, and maintainer-clean.\n\nSigned-off-by: Thomas Bertschinger <bertschinger@lanl.gov>\nFixes: 31e5fc87aebf (\"LU-18876 build: remove MOSTLYCLEANFILES\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nChange-Id: Ie5a7894000f2eee81c0c7a1101615cdbb258cf5e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
